WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
This surging power...

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.073 --> 00:31.160
Black Jack

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.685 --> 00:59.376
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.376 --> 01:01.369
will be there

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
It makes me glad...

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
yokatta

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
That I found my place here.

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.127 --> 01:13.645
Oh WISDOM

01:13.645 --> 01:15.494
will be there

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
I searched for the reason

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
sagashita

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
as long as we're alive.

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.678 --> 01:34.763
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.847 --> 01:37.031
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.183 --> 01:39.794
His name is Black Jack.

01:51.941 --> 01:55.028
Originally "Stradivarius" by Tezuka Osamu

01:51.941 --> 01:55.028
The Violin in the Snowy Field

02:33.053 --> 02:34.550
When's the rescue squad coming?!

02:34.798 --> 02:37.030
We are constantly sending out distress calls.

02:37.220 --> 02:39.430
So the rescue squad will be here any minute.

02:39.764 --> 02:40.973
Please stay calm.

02:41.090 --> 02:43.726
But even the rescue squads can't fly in this weather!

02:43.731 --> 02:44.949
Stop giving us crap!

02:45.061 --> 02:48.522
I don't want to freeze to death here!

02:48.523 --> 02:51.386
Ma'am, please stay calm.

02:51.651 --> 02:52.776
We'll be fine!

02:52.777 --> 02:55.863
Why didn't you change the flight route in the first place?!

02:55.864 --> 02:57.239
Yeah! It was your misjudgement!

02:57.615 --> 02:59.450
This is your fault!

02:59.451 --> 03:01.410
I'll sue you!

03:01.578 --> 03:04.413
Please! Please stay calm!

03:04.414 --> 03:06.540
We really need your cooperation!

03:08.819 --> 03:09.986
The lights went out!

03:10.052 --> 03:10.980
The heaters too!

03:11.004 --> 03:12.588
Help me! Please!

03:12.589 --> 03:15.211
I don't want to die in the middle of nowhere!

03:38.281 --> 03:39.490
He's Morozov!

03:39.491 --> 03:42.743
You're right. That's Alexei Morozov.

04:53.648 --> 04:55.259
Attention please.

04:56.138 --> 05:02.148
We have confirmed that this aircraft is
dangling on the edge of a crevasse.

05:02.522 --> 05:06.065
We don't know when the crevasse will start to widen again.

05:06.536 --> 05:09.363
Fortunately, there is a village nearby.

05:09.664 --> 05:14.793
They have a barn that can shelter all of the passengers.

05:15.503 --> 05:18.380
I would like to lead everyone to that barn now.

05:19.007 --> 05:22.509
Move? Do we have to walk through this blizzard?

05:22.510 --> 05:24.192
It's only about 400 meters away.

05:24.429 --> 05:27.723
You're asking us to walk that far in this blizzard?!

05:28.141 --> 05:29.535
We can't stay here.

05:29.809 --> 05:33.854
Please follow our instructions and disembark.

05:33.855 --> 05:35.981
So we have no choice.

05:35.982 --> 05:37.956
Then we've got to do it.

05:39.319 --> 05:41.445
Please leave your luggage on board.

05:41.446 --> 05:44.198
The wind will blow them away if you carry them with you.

05:44.475 --> 05:46.909
I'd like to take my bag.

05:47.192 --> 05:51.855
I'm sorry, but if we allow one person,
we'll end up having to allow others too.

05:52.207 --> 05:53.499
I'm a doctor.

05:53.500 --> 05:55.626
We may need medical equipment.

05:55.698 --> 05:58.050
We have medical tools too.

05:58.421 --> 06:01.090
And, fortunately, none of the passengers are badly injured.

06:01.549 --> 06:02.841
We don't need to worry.

06:02.842 --> 06:03.967
But...

06:03.968 --> 06:06.057
Please disembark in turn!

06:06.513 --> 06:07.596
Are you a doctor?

06:07.597 --> 06:10.182
He's the best doctor in the world.

06:10.408 --> 06:12.178
That is very reassuring.

06:12.727 --> 06:17.147
I must be thankful for how fortunate I am to be
on board with such a person in this situation.

06:17.482 --> 06:20.845
Your fabulous performance was the best cure here.

06:21.279 --> 06:25.242
You heal people's bodies, and I heal people's hearts.

06:25.573 --> 06:27.822
Perhaps our professions are similar.

06:28.076 --> 06:30.995
We can both save people with our fingers.

06:38.962 --> 06:43.632
Mr. Morozov, please leave your violin on board.

06:43.633 --> 06:46.885
No! He must stay with me no matter where I go!

06:47.103 --> 06:51.181
I'm terribly sorry, but please follow
the captain's instructions.

06:52.392 --> 06:55.144
I just need to make sure he doesn't get blown away, right?

07:01.234 --> 07:02.572
Do you have any problems now?

07:12.487 --> 07:14.300
Man, I'm freezing!

07:15.040 --> 07:18.287
They told us not to bring anything,

07:18.668 --> 07:22.483
but I couldn't leave this behind when I knew it'd be cold.

07:25.425 --> 07:26.550
It's so soothing!

07:26.692 --> 07:28.302
That's not fair!

07:28.303 --> 07:29.553
Let me have a sip!

07:29.671 --> 07:30.288
Hey! Stop it!

07:30.472 --> 07:32.432
It's just one sip!

07:31.514 --> 07:33.307
It's mine!

07:36.353 --> 07:37.436
Pinoco!

08:11.388 --> 08:12.805
Doc!

08:12.806 --> 08:14.730
M-My violin!

08:15.475 --> 08:16.642
Violin!

08:17.936 --> 08:19.895
You mustn't go that way!

08:19.896 --> 08:21.480
My son!

08:21.481 --> 08:22.523
Mr. Morozov!

08:22.524 --> 08:23.649
Son!

08:44.587 --> 08:45.452
Um...

08:45.672 --> 08:47.047
I'm sorry.

08:49.295 --> 08:50.843
Are you going out to die?

08:51.134 --> 08:52.469
Move out of the way.

08:53.013 --> 08:55.674
I can't leave him in the snow.

08:55.932 --> 09:00.436
How do you intend to search for it in this blizzard?

09:00.979 --> 09:02.229
You better give it up.

09:02.402 --> 09:03.814
Give him up?!

09:03.815 --> 09:07.693
You may not know it, but he's not an ordinary instrument!

09:07.961 --> 09:09.895
He's a part of my body!

09:10.405 --> 09:12.276
My fingers are trembling.

09:12.657 --> 09:16.160
They've been trembling and crying
ever since he went missing.

09:17.370 --> 09:18.812
It's because of me.

09:19.080 --> 09:20.539
I'm sorry.

09:23.918 --> 09:26.507
No, it wasn't your fault.

09:26.880 --> 09:29.854
| should have tied him on to me more tightly.

09:30.467 --> 09:33.969
It's my fault that he got blown off my body.

09:34.429 --> 09:37.848
So I must go find him on my own.

09:49.235 --> 09:50.242
You mustn't!

10:03.291 --> 10:04.416
My son!

10:08.588 --> 10:09.580
Mr. Morozov!

10:10.340 --> 10:11.211
This is nonsense!

10:11.591 --> 10:13.651
You'll get frostbite if you continue!

10:14.219 --> 10:17.596
And at your age, it can be fatal!

10:17.931 --> 10:19.283
Please let me go!

10:19.557 --> 10:22.059
I must find him no matter what!

10:22.602 --> 10:25.854
I could treat you if you get frostbite,

10:26.731 --> 10:30.804
but all my medicine and equipment
are in the cargo area of the plane!

10:31.069 --> 10:33.004
We're in no position to go get them!

10:38.284 --> 10:41.328
With this wind chill, your body
temperature will drop quickly!

10:41.329 --> 10:42.871
We must hurry back to the barn.

10:43.498 --> 10:44.873
I can't leave him out there!

10:44.874 --> 10:47.835
He is my only partner.

10:48.378 --> 10:51.502
He is my life itself!

10:59.828 --> 11:01.572
By a single note...

11:02.105 --> 11:03.565
That warm sound.

11:04.185 --> 11:10.774
My life was saved by that single note emanating from him.

11:17.243 --> 11:23.165
As a musician I could go no further,
and I was in despair over my limited talent.

11:23.977 --> 11:30.169
I even thought that I was better off dead
if I couldn't find my own sound.

11:33.131 --> 11:34.256
Hey!

11:43.141 --> 11:46.602
And it was he who rescued me from that despair.

11:47.812 --> 11:51.760
He was waiting there for me the whole time.

11:53.318 --> 11:54.652
Welcome.

12:30.397 --> 12:33.609
That single note saved me,

12:34.025 --> 12:38.070
so I must save that note this time.

12:40.281 --> 12:43.577
No other violin can replace him.

12:44.411 --> 12:51.458
The tonal color is the result of he and
I working together for a long time.

12:52.085 --> 12:54.628
He is my priceless partner.

12:57.332 --> 13:00.759
Let's search for it together once the blizzard clears up.

13:00.760 --> 13:02.553
I'll help too.

13:02.752 --> 13:04.430
I will help too.

13:04.484 --> 13:05.191
Me too.

13:05.515 --> 13:07.766
I'm sure we can find it if we work together.

13:07.836 --> 13:11.979
We won't let the blizzard take away your music!

13:12.731 --> 13:13.928
Thank you.

13:14.774 --> 13:16.912
You should get some rest now.

13:40.775 --> 13:41.235
Oh no!

13:55.899 --> 13:58.651
Doc!

14:49.494 --> 14:51.482
Why did you have to act so recklessly?!

14:52.455 --> 14:55.290
He's calling for me.

14:56.084 --> 14:57.668
Asking me to find him.

14:58.211 --> 15:02.881
Once he freezes, that tone will never come back.

15:03.675 --> 15:05.765
The varnish will crack.

15:06.261 --> 15:12.391
He knows it, so he's calling out to me for help.

15:12.644 --> 15:16.558
All I can hear is the scream of your fingers!

15:22.527 --> 15:23.736
Doc!

15:33.204 --> 15:36.498
Doctor, here are the medical goods
that were stocked on board.

15:43.794 --> 15:45.549
Please save him.

15:45.967 --> 15:48.719
There's nothing I can use here, even if I wanted to.

15:48.720 --> 15:52.765
Why didn't you let him take his bag?

15:53.141 --> 15:55.000
Is it in the baggage compartment?

15:56.311 --> 15:57.770
I'll go get it!

15:57.937 --> 15:58.771
Hold it.

15:58.953 --> 15:59.898
I'll go.

16:00.523 --> 16:03.717
You, stay here and massage Mr. Morozov's
fingers while they're immersed in water.

16:04.194 --> 16:07.127
Start at a low temperature and raise it gradually.

16:07.634 --> 16:08.301
Can you handle that?

16:09.574 --> 16:10.908
Aye-aye.

16:11.284 --> 16:12.304
I'll come with you.

16:12.535 --> 16:14.745
I'm sure the fuselage will have been buried in snow.

16:14.746 --> 16:16.422
Maybe having more people will help.

16:18.541 --> 16:21.346
We'll push this as we walk.

16:22.003 --> 16:27.059
That's what my grandpa always did when he
absolutely had to go out in such weather.

16:27.509 --> 16:28.550
Right, Grandpa?

16:31.346 --> 16:32.746
We're veering to the right!

16:33.098 --> 16:34.593
Push the right side more!

16:41.147 --> 16:42.823
Straight against the wind!

16:49.571 --> 16:50.466
Does it hurt?

16:50.490 --> 16:53.219
No, I can't feel anything.

17:02.669 --> 17:04.856
The lower half is completely buried!

17:05.588 --> 17:06.892
Oh my word!

17:07.173 --> 17:10.426
We can't enter the cargo area from outside like that!

17:10.427 --> 17:11.647
Then we'll enter from the cabin!

17:26.318 --> 17:27.067
Watch out!

17:27.068 --> 17:28.277
Step back, Doctor!

17:55.430 --> 17:56.418
Doctor.

17:57.724 --> 17:58.974
Thank you.

17:59.434 --> 18:03.060
I did nothing worth being thanked for.

18:03.688 --> 18:06.322
I couldn't do anything.

18:06.941 --> 18:10.944
Would the outcome have been different
if you had proper equipment?

18:11.696 --> 18:12.896
I believe so.

18:13.782 --> 18:14.756
I'm sorry.

18:15.417 --> 18:19.355
You mustn't let go of your most prized possession.

18:19.871 --> 18:22.219
Now we know.

18:22.667 --> 18:24.544
Both you and I.

18:34.094 --> 18:36.808
Are those my fingers?

18:37.097 --> 18:38.222
They are.

18:38.223 --> 18:39.530
Can I see them?

18:46.562 --> 18:47.909
I'm sorry.

18:48.566 --> 18:52.379
I forced such harsh work on you for such a long time.

18:52.696 --> 18:53.782
Thank you.

18:54.990 --> 18:57.280
What would you like to do with them?

18:59.536 --> 19:02.272
Please bury them beneath these snowy fields.

19:02.747 --> 19:06.156
My Stradivarius is somewhere nearby too.

19:06.950 --> 19:08.990
I want to let them rest together.

19:15.010 --> 19:17.779
Why are you saddened?

19:18.221 --> 19:20.019
All music must end.

19:20.974 --> 19:24.409
The music ends when the conductor puts down his baton.

19:24.978 --> 19:27.229
That's all.

19:27.564 --> 19:32.405
My music had its final movement here.

19:32.986 --> 19:38.365
I can only be satisfied that I gave
a fine performance in the end.

19:45.749 --> 19:49.444
The sound you create once shall never ceases to exist.

21:43.366 --> 21:47.035
The sound you create once shall never cease to exist.

22:10.550 --> 22:17.556
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.550 --> 22:17.556
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.557 --> 22:24.729
Only look straight at me.

22:17.557 --> 22:24.729
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.774 --> 22:32.031
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.774 --> 22:32.031
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.032 --> 22:42.541
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.032 --> 22:42.541
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.542 --> 22:47.922
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.542 --> 22:47.922
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.923 --> 22:57.306
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.923 --> 22:53.128
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.583 --> 22:57.307
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.307 --> 23:08.067
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.307 --> 23:08.067
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.068 --> 23:13.155
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.068 --> 23:13.155
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.156 --> 23:26.126
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.156 --> 23:26.126
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.127 --> 23:33.050
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.127 --> 23:33.050
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.051 --> 23:43.936
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.051 --> 23:36.984
sora no hate tooku

23:37.077 --> 23:43.877
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.136 --> 24:15.125
The Robin & the Boy

23:46.503 --> 23:47.503
A bird!

23:47.529 --> 23:48.889
The bird has money in its beak!

23:49.109 --> 23:51.248
That's a Japanese robin.

23:51.503 --> 23:52.703
Japanese robin?

23:53.136 --> 23:56.316
It's said that robins bring happiness,

23:56.800 --> 23:58.661
but I never knew that they brought money too.

24:00.261 --> 24:01.594
It must be his kidneys.

24:01.927 --> 24:02.927
Who are you?

24:03.652 --> 24:04.905
I'll get it!

24:05.919 --> 24:07.846
It's now over ¥50,000.

24:08.312 --> 24:10.852
Mysterious money coming to
the Black Jack residence...

24:11.904 --> 24:14.231
Next Karte - The Robin & the Boy.

24:16.108 --> 24:17.859
Karte NG...

24:23.966 --> 24:24.648
Cut!
